<!--
  MTK PowerHAL per-application boost whitelist for k50sv1_64_bsp.

  Deliberately empty.

  Stock ships a seven-entry table naming com.tencent.tmgp.sgame,
  com.tencent.tmgp.sgamece, com.tencent.tmgp.pubgmhd, com.ss.android.ugc.aweme,
  com.smile.gifmaker, com.taobao.taobao and com.imangi.templerun2. None of them
  is installed on this build, and every frequency in it (1950000) is an OPP
  this part does not have, so the table is inert either way. It is not carried
  forward: a whitelist that names applications the image does not ship is a
  maintenance trap, and the generic boosts in powerscntbl.xml already cover
  every hint the AOSP framework sends.

  libpowerhal prefers /data/vendor/powerhal/power_whitelist_cfg.xml over this
  file, so a per-application experiment can be dropped in at runtime without a
  rebuild. Add real entries here only for an application that is actually
  installed and measurably helped, and only with OPPs from
  /proc/ppm/dump_cluster_{0,1}_dvfs_table.
-->
<WHITELIST>
    <PerfService>
    </PerfService>
</WHITELIST>
